  "caption_groups": [
    {
      "start": 0.9604747267365955,
      "end": 3.587714642732244,
      "text": "Beavers live in freshwater ecosystems such"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.602368346007131,
      "end": 6.156198844635315,
      "text": "as rivers, streams, lakes and ponds"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.185553593918748,
      "end": 7.374427703145401,
      "text": "across the landscape."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.324357672864542,
      "end": 11.423218865006083,
      "text": "In Europe, beavers were reduced to"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.452573614289514,
      "end": 14.035757734993187,
      "text": "fragmented populations, with combined"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.050411438268075,
      "end": 16.707006103547155,
      "text": "population numbers being estimated at small"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.721659806822043,
      "end": 17.294093198760184,
      "text": "totals."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.779377908999475,
      "end": 21.39191677898658,
      "text": "Combined population numbers were estimated"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.42127152827001,
      "end": 23.71091266497114,
      "text": "at twelve hundred individuals for the Rhone"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.725613710979687,
      "end": 25.354804550626042,
      "text": "of France and other regions."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.827642630745235,
      "end": 29.631008788025586,
      "text": "The concept became popular in conservation,"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.968560224586447,
      "end": 31.524388989598993,
      "text": "and was deployed in a range of"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.55369639614877,
      "end": 33.56449446764796,
      "text": "contexts to engender support."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.065278287120314,
      "end": 37.45768359047234,
      "text": "This framework was mobilized to engender"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.487037212547826,
      "end": 38.9841102634678,
      "text": "support for conservation,"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.36571749532063,
      "end": 41.449877641453625,
      "text": "especially where human activities had"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.47923239073706,
      "end": 42.961604395648486,
      "text": "damaged ecosystems."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.466192541932585,
      "end": 46.990715634010996,
      "text": "In addition, wolves often kept animals"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.020023040560766,
      "end": 48.98681265950164,
      "text": "from grazing in riparian areas,"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.29501047398701,
      "end": 51.10028133939235,
      "text": "which protected beavers from food"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.12963496146784,
      "end": 51.90754934397412,
      "text": "encroachment."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.407205955502235,
      "end": 55.34459348242601,
      "text": "The connectivity of streams to their"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.37394935891739,
      "end": 57.67829041441912,
      "text": "adjacent floodplain along their entire"
    },
    {
      "start": 57.70764516370255,
      "end": 59.54226965118338,
      "text": "length plays an important role in"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.55697069719193,
      "end": 60.42294820034056,
      "text": "equilibrium."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.942424509151934,
      "end": 64.52565597258926,
      "text": "Stream restoration or river restoration"
    },
    {
      "start": 64.54030967586415,
      "end": 66.31627200751178,
      "text": "is a set of activities that aim"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.3455805412695,
      "end": 68.5178511507785,
      "text": "to improve the environmental health."
    }
  ],
